# The hosts an operating system checks to decide whether a network works.
#
# These are reachable to UNREGISTERED devices and are deliberately NOT
# redirected to the portal. That costs the automatic sign-in pop-up, and buys
# something worth more: macOS marks the network "connected", so Safari is
# willing to make requests at all.
#
# With these intercepted, macOS flags the interface as captive, and then
# refuses to let the browser reach the very host the student needs to sign in
# at -- the sign-in becomes impossible rather than merely undiscovered.
# Verified: DNS resolved, and not one packet left the Mac.
#
# Set CAPTIVE_POPUP="1" in classnet.conf to restore interception. The pop-up
# returns, and so does that trap.
captive.apple.com
captive.g.aaplimg.com
www.apple.com
connectivitycheck.gstatic.com
www.msftconnecttest.com
detectportal.firefox.com
network-test.debian.org
